From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] spi: stm32-qspi: allow an explicit XIP handoff

An XIP kernel needs the QSPI controller to remain in memory-mapped mode
after U-Boot has loaded its device tree. Permit the board environment to
request that one-way handoff. The default remains to abort memory-mapped
reads, preserving the established zImage and flash-update behavior.

The XIP boot command sets the variable immediately before its final small
read at offset zero and does not persist the environment. Program DLR for
the complete aperture during that operation so the controller does not set
transfer-complete after the small staging copy. Keep the controller enabled
when the generic SPI layer releases the bus so subsequent AHB fetches work,
and change the QSPI MPU region from Device to executable normal memory. Keep
the MPU enabled while updating that otherwise-unused region: disabling it at
runtime would make cached SDRAM stack accesses use the default Device mapping.
Use region 3 because Linux installs its XIP ROM mapping into that same region;
using Linux's background region 1 would remove execute permission midway
through the kernel's early MPU setup.

Signed-off-by: hIRoic Linux PoC <noreply@localhost>
---
 drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c b/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c
--- a/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/stm32_qspi.c
@@ -13,0 +14 @@
+#include <env.h>
@@ -25,0 +27 @@
+#include <asm/armv7_mpu.h>
@@ -26,0 +29 @@
+#include <asm/barriers.h>
@@ -281,0 +283 @@ static int stm32_qspi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave,
+	bool leave_mapped;
@@ -296,0 +299,2 @@ static int stm32_qspi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave,
+	leave_mapped = mode == STM32_QSPI_CCR_MEM_MAP &&
+			env_get_yesno("qspi_leave_mapped") == 1;
@@ -299 +303,2 @@ static int stm32_qspi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave,
-		writel(op->data.nbytes - 1, &priv->regs->dlr);
+		writel(leave_mapped ? priv->mm_size - 1 :
+		       op->data.nbytes - 1, &priv->regs->dlr);
@@ -353 +359,18 @@ static int stm32_qspi_exec_op(struct spi_slave *slave,
-	if (ret || mode == STM32_QSPI_CCR_MEM_MAP)
+	if (!ret && leave_mapped) {
+		struct mpu_region_config xip_region = {
+			.start_addr = 0x90000000,
+			.region_no = REGION_3,
+			.xn = XN_DIS,
+			.ap = PRIV_RO_USR_RO,
+			.mr_attr = O_I_NON_CACHEABLE,
+			.reg_size = REGION_256MB,
+		};
+
+		dsb();
+		mpu_config(&xip_region);
+		dsb();
+		isb();
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	if (ret || mode == STM32_QSPI_CCR_MEM_MAP)
@@ -481,0 +504,3 @@ static int stm32_qspi_release_bus(struct udevice *dev)
+	if (env_get_yesno("qspi_leave_mapped") == 1)
+		return 0;
+
-- 
